{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Stress, such as that caused by an approaching deadline, can indeed worsen acid reflux symptoms. Stress and anxiety do not directly cause acid reflux but can increase your perception of symptoms and may lead to behaviors (like eating late or unhealthy foods) that trigger reflux.\n\nFor over-the-counter (OTC) medications, several options are available to help manage acid reflux:\n- **Antacids**: These neutralize stomach acid and provide quick relief (e.g., Tums, Maalox).\n- **H2 blockers**: These reduce acid production (e.g., Ranitidine).\n- **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)**: These are stronger acid reducers (e.g., Prilosec, Nexium). However, for young adults, they are not usually recommended as a first treatment due to potential long-term side effects.\n- **Alginates**: These form a barrier to prevent acid from reaching the esophagus.\n\nIt is advisable to focus on lifestyle changes\u2014such as eating earlier, maintaining a healthy weight, and managing stress\u2014before relying on medications. If you decide to use OTC options, use them as directed and consult your healthcare provider if symptoms persist.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0005-31-05925:5": 21.7467041015625, "clueweb22-en0007-79-07412:8": 21.561485290527344, "clueweb22-en0029-30-08058:1": 21.522977828979492, "clueweb22-en0042-95-07832:10": 21.207998275756836, "clueweb22-en0003-41-13624:7": 21.16023063659668, "clueweb22-en0017-09-02813:0": 21.075578689575195, "clueweb22-en0004-88-08290:1": 21.045934677124023, "clueweb22-en0028-25-12784:3": 20.92291259765625, "clueweb22-en0012-13-07696:11": 20.868852615356445, "clueweb22-en0039-92-15038:12": 20.850135803222656}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I eat dinner late at night.", "I have gained weight recently because I stopped exercising for the last 6 months.", "I spend too much time on my phone.", "I want to change my lifest