{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "2-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Chardonnay wines with hazelnut notes are often associated with regions that use oak aging and specific winemaking techniques. In particular, oaked Chardonnays from areas with a reputation for meticulous winemaking, such as Burgundy in France and select producers in Italy, can develop rich flavors of hazelnut, caramel, and honey. For example, in Piedmont, Italy, renowned for its high-quality hazelnuts and wines, winemakers sometimes collaborate with local producers to enhance these delicate nutty flavors.\n\nIf you are interested in dessert wines, Tuscany\u2019s Vin Santo is another notable option. This sweet, full-bodied wine offers pronounced notes of caramel, hazelnut, and honey, and is traditionally served with biscotti.\n\nGiven your preference for gentle wines, an oaked Chardonnay or Vin Santo from Italy\u2014particularly Tuscany or Piedmont\u2014would be an excellent and enjoyable choice to explore hazelnut flavors. Sampling different wines from these regions will help you discover which style best matches your taste.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0009-51-09023:7": 25.22235107421875, "clueweb22-en0029-65-12315:3": 25.01374053955078, "clueweb22-en0009-51-09023:6": 24.22161102294922, "clueweb22-en0010-43-10077:1": 23.75322723388672, "clueweb22-en0012-13-11509:11": 23.726593017578125, "clueweb22-en0027-16-15923:2": 23.536455154418945, "clueweb22-en0027-16-15923:1": 23.293941497802734, "clueweb22-en0042-98-18421:9": 23.2320556640625, "clueweb22-en0005-90-17284:16": 23.139314651489258, "clueweb22-en0013-86-10584:6": 23.131813049316406}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I like to try something new here and then.", "I occasionally experience mild acid reflux and prefer beverages that are gentle on the stomach."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0009-51-09023:7": 25.22235107421875, "clueweb22-en0029-65-12315:3": 25.01374053955078, "clu