{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Of course. For taping an A2 pulley injury, it\u2019s important to use a method that limits finger bending and prevents crimping, which aids recovery. Here\u2019s a summarized approach:\n\n1. Use athletic finger tape.\n2. Start by wrapping the tape around the base of the finger (just below the first joint, where the A2 pulley is located).\n3. Create a \u201ctape bridge\u201d over the joint to provide support and limit excessive bending.\n4. Wrap the tape snugly but not too tight\u2014circulation should not be restricted.\n5. Make sure the finger is in a neutral, slightly bent position while taping.\n6. Retape frequently, especially if the tape loosens or stretches during climbing.\n\nSome experts recommend H-taping for added support, but keep in mind that taping is most effective when combined with rest and a gradual return to climbing. Also, avoid taping too tightly and change the tape regularly to prevent skin irritation or infection. \n\nIf you have any swelling or ongoing pain, use over-the-counter pain relievers and monitor your symptoms.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0019-33-03699:9": 22.417322158813477, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 21.148157119750977, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 20.890527725219727, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 20.68520164489746, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 20.412519454956055, "clueweb22-en0032-68-13591:11": 20.362056732177734, "clueweb22-en0006-50-11612:1": 20.30402183532715, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 19.967859268188477, "clueweb22-en0003-54-05279:4": 19.763532638549805, "clueweb22-en0007-53-17747:10": 19.757240295410156}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years.", "I climb outdoors."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0019-33-03699:9": 22.417322158813477, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 21.148157119750977, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 20.89052772521972