{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "4-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "With four months to prepare, you have an excellent amount of time to build up safely and confidently for your 10 km run. Here\u2019s how to approach your training:\n\n1. **Progressive Training:** Start by gradually increasing your weekly mileage and the length of your long run. For example, increase your long run by about 1 km each week for three weeks, then take a lighter week for recovery before resuming the increase. This helps prevent injury and builds endurance.\n\n2. **Weekly Structure:** Aim for 4\u20135 running sessions per week. Alternate between easy runs, interval sessions (speedwork), a tempo run, and a long run. Make sure to include at least one rest day or a cross-training session (like cycling or swimming).\n\n3. **Consistency:** The key is regularity rather than intensity, especially if you are not fully confident in your fitness level. Stick to a routine, listen to your body, and adjust as needed.\n\n4. **Cross-training & Rest:** Incorporate non-running activities or extra rest on certain days to maintain overall fitness and help recovery.\n\nThis approach allows you to steadily improve your endurance and speed in time for your race, without overwhelming yourself.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0040-97-13459:4": 24.030366897583008, "clueweb22-en0015-82-16999:7": 23.981386184692383, "clueweb22-en0043-38-10661:12": 23.829906463623047, "clueweb22-en0043-14-06960:4": 23.814407348632812, "clueweb22-en0033-69-15716:1": 23.460899353027344, "clueweb22-en0007-67-06242:0": 23.46050453186035, "clueweb22-en0030-25-07522:12": 23.433822631835938, "clueweb22-en0004-91-11430:18": 23.344402313232422, "clueweb22-en0031-72-03270:12": 23.34316062927246, "clueweb22-en0027-63-10803:16": 23.239479064941406}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not very confident in my fitness level.", "I live in Spain."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0