{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "While orange juice provides vitamins and antioxidants, it is also high in naturally occurring sugars and lacks the fiber found in whole fruits. Your body responds to sugar in orange juice much like it does to table sugar, so consuming large amounts can impact blood sugar levels.\n\nRegarding sweeteners, natural and processed sugars\u2014including those found in juices, honey, and agave\u2014are high in calories and can negatively affect health if consumed excessively. Some processed options, like agave nectar, are actually higher in fructose than table sugar and should be used with caution.\n\nArtificial and low-calorie sweeteners such as stevia, erythritol, and monk fruit are often recommended as alternatives. They provide sweetness with little or no impact on blood sugar and contain few, if any, calories. However, some artificial sweeteners (like Aspartame or Sucralose) are present in diet drinks and low-sugar products; they are generally considered safe in moderation, though some people may experience sensitivities.\n\nFor the healthiest approach, prioritize whole fruits for natural sweetness and fiber, and use low- or no-calorie sweeteners like stevia or erythritol if you need to reduce sugar intake. Enjoy orange juice in moderation as part of a balanced diet.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0018-16-07572:15": 25.5792179107666, "clueweb22-en0013-96-08808:5": 25.036441802978516, "clueweb22-en0019-56-15014:0": 24.11271095275879, "clueweb22-en0015-67-00598:3": 23.93149757385254, "clueweb22-en0030-55-13575:9": 23.872440338134766, "clueweb22-en0040-54-09684:8": 23.77081298828125, "clueweb22-en0018-11-09908:5": 23.591848373413086, "clueweb22-en0003-42-19627:10": 23.251691818237305, "clueweb22-en0007-90-10506:18": 23.193851470947266, "clueweb22-en0011-89-08296:7": 23.179248809814453}, "ptkb_provenance": ["Sometimes I drink 