{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_7", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Breastfeeding is highly recommended for at least the first six months of your baby\u2019s life, as it provides optimal nutrition, supports your baby\u2019s immune system, and promotes healthy development. It also benefits you by supporting uterine recovery, reducing postpartum bleeding, burning extra calories, and lowering the risk of certain diseases, such as breast and ovarian cancers. Breastfeeding can also foster emotional bonding with your baby, delay the return of menstruation, and may help with postpartum weight loss.\n\nFor mothers with specific dietary concerns, such as getting enough calcium, it is important to ensure your diet is balanced and rich in nutrients while breastfeeding. If you have any particular health conditions or dietary restrictions, or if you are considering combining breastfeeding with bottle feeding, consulting a healthcare provider for personalized advice is recommended. \n\nOverall, breastfeeding offers significant health, emotional, and practical advantages for both you and your baby.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-85-06393:10": 22.119487762451172, "clueweb22-en0012-14-02860:1": 21.281661987304688, "clueweb22-en0044-25-13413:1": 21.158483505249023, "clueweb22-en0005-46-00778:1": 21.030603408813477, "clueweb22-en0029-81-00629:2": 21.01968002319336, "clueweb22-en0005-16-07992:0": 20.961538314819336, "clueweb22-en0028-89-17605:1": 20.893569946289062, "clueweb22-en0044-25-13413:4": 20.836475372314453, "clueweb22-en0025-29-00546:2": 20.77495574951172, "clueweb22-en0040-60-11237:17": 20.753774642944336}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I think I don't get enough calcium, and I am worried about it.", "I like eating cake as a snack with coffee, and I bake cakes every week.", "I enjoy watching cake decorating competitions on TV shows.", "Sometimes I drink fresh orange juice in the afternoon.", "I eat ja