{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "It is completely natural to feel concerned about your baby crying\u2014many new parents feel the same way. Babies cry for many reasons, such as hunger, discomfort, tiredness, or simply needing comfort. Crying is a normal part of a baby\u2019s development and is also a way for them to communicate their needs.\n\nIn the early weeks, babies may want to breastfeed very frequently, sometimes seeming unsettled or fussy even after feeding. This can be exhausting and emotionally challenging, but it is perfectly normal. Sometimes, despite your best efforts to comfort and feed your baby, crying may still occur, especially during certain times of the day like early evening.\n\nRemember, it is okay if your baby cries sometimes. Trying different comforting techniques\u2014such as breastfeeding, holding your baby close, using a sling, or gentle background noise\u2014may help soothe them. Most babies become more settled after the first 12\u201314 weeks. It\u2019s also important to look after your own well-being as you adjust to life after childbirth. You are already showing great care and concern, which is a wonderful start to being a loving mum.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0035-37-13460:2": 29.351810455322266, "clueweb22-en0022-68-06664:3": 29.008085250854492, "clueweb22-en0002-10-04388:5": 28.66974449157715, "clueweb22-en0038-63-05257:16": 28.608299255371094, "clueweb22-en0036-41-19433:8": 28.569150924682617, "clueweb22-en0023-66-12715:0": 28.23955535888672, "clueweb22-en0016-37-09514:12": 28.038190841674805, "clueweb22-en0022-68-06664:2": 27.8579158782959, "clueweb22-en0044-04-04492:13": 27.6903133392334, "clueweb22-en0036-41-19433:7": 27.565879821777344}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0035-37-13460:2": 29.351810455322266, "clueweb22-en0022-68-06664:3": 29.008085250854492, "clueweb22-en0002-10-04388:5": 28