{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Microneedling is a less intensive alternative to CO2 laser resurfacing and may be a suitable option for your goals\u2014especially considering your interest in minimal downtime. This procedure uses tiny needles to create micro-injuries in the skin, which stimulate collagen production and skin cell renewal. Over time, this can lead to improvements in dark spots, uneven tone, and visible pores, while providing a smoother overall texture.\n\nMost people experience only mild redness and swelling for a day or two after microneedling, and makeup can usually be worn again soon after. Results develop gradually over several months, and multiple sessions are often needed for the best outcome. Side effects are generally mild, and the risk of pigmentation changes or significant discomfort is much lower than with CO2 lasers.\n\nGiven your routine use of vitamin C, retinol, and AHA/BHA, microneedling can complement your existing regimen, helping you achieve a more even and refined complexion with minimal disruption to your daily life.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0036-10-01168:8": 19.018848419189453, "clueweb22-en0026-58-09443:6": 18.90470314025879, "clueweb22-en0036-10-01168:9": 18.274158477783203, "clueweb22-en0017-43-06405:11": 18.247547149658203, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:6": 18.245574951171875, "clueweb22-en0046-16-08470:5": 18.239669799804688, "clueweb22-en0046-16-08470:6": 18.238840103149414, "clueweb22-en0009-27-04860:7": 18.110111236572266, "clueweb22-en0016-80-15701:8": 17.93340492248535, "clueweb22-en0038-90-16597:4": 17.903104782104492}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I use AHA BHA serum once a week.", "I am a 40-ye