{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_12", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "After microneedling, it is important to temporarily adjust your skincare routine to support healing and minimize irritation. While salicylic acid is effective for oily skin, its use immediately after microneedling is not recommended. Salicylic acid, being a chemical exfoliant, can increase dryness and irritation, especially when the skin barrier is already compromised from the treatment. It is advisable to avoid applying your salicylic acid face wash and other strong exfoliants for at least 24 to 48 hours following your microneedling session.\n\nFor your scalp and hair, if you use shampoos or treatments containing salicylic acid, similar caution is advised. Wait until any scalp sensitivity or redness subsides before resuming these products to prevent discomfort or additional irritation.\n\nDuring the initial healing period, focus on gentle cleansing and prioritize hydrating ingredients, such as hyaluronic acid, which are safe and beneficial post-microneedling. Once your skin and scalp have recovered\u2014typically after two days\u2014you may gradually reintroduce salicylic acid-based products, monitoring for any signs of irritation. Always follow your provider\u2019s aftercare instructions for the best results and safety.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0026-00-10032:6": 37.63264465332031, "clueweb22-en0002-73-05205:4": 37.45622634887695, "clueweb22-en0000-59-08693:0": 37.40778732299805, "clueweb22-en0031-35-14563:6": 36.263267517089844, "clueweb22-en0007-46-03084:7": 36.171382904052734, "clueweb22-en0026-00-10032:7": 35.7784538269043, "clueweb22-en0033-27-06224:11": 35.72459411621094, "clueweb22-en0031-83-00793:5": 35.48385238647461, "clueweb22-en0000-59-08693:9": 35.4560661315918, "clueweb22-en0033-27-06224:10": 35.34198760986328}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I use vitamin C and Retinol every day in my morning routine.", "I h