{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_1", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. Managing ADHD at work involves a combination of strategic adjustments and support. Since you work in an office and have a sedentary lifestyle, consider the following tailored strategies:\n\n1. **Minimize Distractions**: Seek a quieter workspace if possible, and control interruptions like calls and emails to help maintain focus.\n\n2. **Time Management**: Use electronic reminders and calendars to track tasks and deadlines. Breaking tasks into smaller, manageable steps can also prevent feeling overwhelmed.\n\n3. **Organization**: Regularly clear your workspace and organize documents to reduce distractions. Tracking your spending and removing yourself from unnecessary mailing lists can help manage impulsivity.\n\n4. **Proactive Communication**: If comfortable, consider disclosing your diagnosis to your employer to discuss potential accommodations, such as flexible deadlines or modified work environments.\n\n5. **Professional Support**: ADHD coaching or therapy can help you develop personalized strategies for managing symptoms like impulsivity, distractibility, and organization.\n\n6. **Lifestyle Adjustments**: Even with a sedentary role, scheduling short movement breaks can boost focus and productivity.\n\nRemember, managing ADHD is an ongoing process, and seeking support is a sign of strength. If you need further guidance, consider consulting a professional experienced in ADHD management.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0044-40-11164:3": 28.79811668395996, "clueweb22-en0035-93-06191:0": 28.356233596801758, "clueweb22-en0008-99-02137:2": 27.71986198425293, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:7": 27.270809173583984, "clueweb22-en0022-36-16118:14": 27.1383113861084, "clueweb22-en0001-96-19542:14": 26.671165466308594, "clueweb22-en0022-36-16118:13": 26.66651725769043, "clueweb22-en0040-18-11535:4": 26.308677673339844, "cluewe