{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Your experience of jumping between tasks and struggling to finish them is very common, especially with ADHD. Research shows that multitasking actually reduces productivity because the brain cannot fully focus on more than one task at a time. Each time you switch tasks, your brain loses efficiency, making it harder to complete anything and increasing feelings of overwhelm.\n\nA helpful strategy is to focus on one small task at a time. By giving your full attention to a single step, you\u2019ll be more likely to finish it and feel a sense of accomplishment, which can reduce anxiety and the urge to switch tasks. It may help to work in short bursts\u2014set a timer for 10\u201320 minutes, pick just one task, and give yourself permission to ignore everything else until the timer ends.\n\nAdditionally, proactively prioritizing your tasks\u2014deciding in advance what is most important\u2014can help you stay on track and avoid feeling overwhelmed. Would you like guidance on how to set up a simple prioritization system or tips for working in focused bursts?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-56-13732:6": 31.350942611694336, "clueweb22-en0006-19-06555:4": 31.151325225830078, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:1": 30.122865676879883, "clueweb22-en0042-19-09714:3": 30.077850341796875, "clueweb22-en0018-70-09628:7": 29.701404571533203, "clueweb22-en0032-63-05053:2": 29.56853675842285, "clueweb22-en0006-19-06555:5": 29.369129180908203, "clueweb22-en0021-97-20067:15": 29.3381404876709, "clueweb22-en0004-59-16742:0": 29.139596939086914, "clueweb22-en0035-32-01549:1": 29.036029815673828}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I love it when it is quiet.", "I often daydream.", "I sometimes suddenly feel tired.", "Sometimes I feel awkward when others are around."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0024-56-13732:6": 31.350942611694336, "clueweb22-en0006-19-06555:4":