{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. One proven method for managing focus when you feel pulled between multiple tasks is the Pomodoro Technique. Here\u2019s how it works: \n\nYou select one task to focus on and set a timer for 25 minutes. During this interval, you work solely on that single task, avoiding any multitasking. When the timer goes off, you take a short 5-minute break. This cycle\u201425 minutes of focused work followed by a short break\u2014can be repeated several times. If your attention starts to fade or you feel tempted to switch tasks, remind yourself that you only need to stick with the current task until the timer rings.\n\nThis approach works well in an office setting because it helps you develop discipline, minimizes the inefficiency of task-switching, and makes large workloads feel more manageable. Over time, using this structure can help you maintain momentum and complete tasks more efficiently. Would you like tips on setting up your workspace or using timers effectively?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0024-63-00484:10": 16.36992835998535, "clueweb22-en0016-22-09673:11": 15.99685287475586, "clueweb22-en0017-07-18143:5": 15.98186206817627, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 15.947203636169434, "clueweb22-en0017-61-15257:19": 15.931446075439453, "clueweb22-en0025-68-10509:7": 15.900794982910156, "clueweb22-en0045-81-04179:18": 15.821744918823242, "clueweb22-en0001-66-11662:19": 15.802192687988281, "clueweb22-en0001-49-04668:16": 15.574323654174805, "clueweb22-en0013-15-15509:3": 15.485496520996094}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0024-63-00484:10": 16.36992835998535, "clueweb22-en0016-22-09673:11": 15.99685287475586, "clueweb22-en0017-07-18143:5": 15.98186206817627, "clueweb22-en0001-30-00712:21": 15.947203636169434, "clueweb22-en0017-61-15257:19": 15.931446075439453, "clueweb22-en0025-