{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Thank you for clarifying. Meetings, even in a quiet office, can indeed be a significant source of distraction\u2014especially when they interrupt periods of deep focus or hyperfocus. To minimize their disruptive effect, you might consider these strategies:\n\n- Block out time for focused work and clearly communicate your priorities to colleagues, so unnecessary meetings or ad hoc requests do not intrude on your most productive periods.\n- When possible, request that meetings be scheduled together within certain time blocks, rather than scattered throughout the day, to help maintain longer stretches of uninterrupted work.\n- Before entering a meeting, take a moment to mentally \u201cpark\u201d your current task\u2014jot down where you left off so you can easily return to it afterwards.\n- Limit distractions within meetings themselves by minimizing background noise and silencing mobile devices, ensuring that the meeting stays on topic and is as brief and effective as possible.\n\nBy setting boundaries and planning your workday around necessary meetings, you can better protect your focus and maintain productivity. If you\u2019d like more tailored suggestions, feel free to share your typical meeting schedule or challenges.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0014-90-13549:13": 19.768043518066406, "clueweb22-en0007-81-09685:15": 19.564678192138672, "clueweb22-en0032-18-03467:8": 19.561899185180664, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:3": 19.558944702148438, "clueweb22-en0044-40-08170:4": 19.527463912963867, "clueweb22-en0023-18-01227:13": 19.38103485107422, "clueweb22-en0030-05-00631:2": 19.288284301757812, "clueweb22-en0039-78-02488:3": 19.20878791809082, "clueweb22-en0020-66-00848:8": 19.108186721801758, "clueweb22-en0020-78-10594:14": 19.020221710205078}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I love it when it is quiet.", "I work in an office.", "I have