{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. Since you use a mountain bike on forest trails and rough paths and value comfort over speed, it's important to choose a saddle that suits your riding style and needs. \n\nPerformance saddles are narrow and minimally padded, designed for advanced riders who prioritize maximum thigh movement and power transfer. However, these can feel uncomfortable, especially on long or bumpy rides. Given your preference for comfort and casual riding, a comfort saddle\u2014wider and more padded\u2014may be more suitable. Comfort saddles are designed to balance support and ease, especially for longer rides and varied terrain, though excessive padding can sometimes cause discomfort if it doesn\u2019t fit your body properly.\n\nFor mountain biking, select a saddle that matches your anatomy and riding posture, offers sufficient padding, and is made from durable, weather-resistant materials like synthetic leather or Kevlar. Features such as proper airflow and sturdy rails (steel or alloy) are also important for riding in different weather and terrain conditions.\n\nIt\u2019s a good idea to test a few different saddles to find one that best fits your body and comfort preferences.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:8": 36.20151138305664, "clueweb22-en0019-38-14530:7": 33.77382278442383, "clueweb22-en0024-11-16907:7": 33.07439422607422, "clueweb22-en0024-67-05830:1": 32.94113540649414, "clueweb22-en0025-01-00145:12": 32.72443771362305, "clueweb22-en0007-52-02129:7": 32.601463317871094, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:3": 32.330257415771484, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:4": 32.26416778564453, "clueweb22-en0025-27-04261:3": 32.07571029663086, "clueweb22-en0007-05-17998:14": 31.995454788208008}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I value comfort over speed.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I recently moved to a city with more hills and rough paths.", 