{"metadata": {"team_id": "guidance", "run_id": "agg_false-qrec-mse", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Certainly. To open your bike chain, first check if it has a master link\u2014a special link that looks different from the others, often with a clip or a slot. If your chain has a master link, you can open it by pressing the two plates together and sliding them apart. If there is no master link, you\u2019ll need to use your chain breaker tool.\n\nTo use the chain breaker:\n1. Place the chain in the slot of the chain tool, aligning the pin of the tool with a chain pin you want to push out.\n2. Turn the handle of the chain breaker slowly, pushing the chain pin most of the way out (but not all the way, to avoid losing it).\n3. Once the pin is almost out, you can separate the chain.\n\nWhen you\u2019re ready to reconnect the chain, you can use the tool again to push the pin back in, or use a master link if you have one. Take your time and make sure the links are not stiff after reconnecting. If you find any step difficult, consider consulting a professional.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:5": 24.6846981048584, "clueweb22-en0010-22-02970:14": 24.15103530883789, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:6": 24.150768280029297, "clueweb22-en0008-58-03477:3": 23.963802337646484, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:13": 23.92272186279297, "clueweb22-en0000-57-03556:5": 23.656103134155273, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:14": 23.650745391845703, "clueweb22-en0043-42-13993:0": 23.613534927368164, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:11": 23.548124313354492, "clueweb22-en0020-78-15858:3": 23.44708824157715}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am not really handy with DIY.", "I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0022-62-09551:5": 24.6846981048584, "clueweb22-en0010-22-02970:14": 24.15103530883789, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:6": 24.150768280029297, "clueweb22-en0008-58-03477:3": 23.963802337646484, "clueweb22-en0019-